WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.430
On the high west Highlands, over 3,500
millimetres of rain falls in a year.

2
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:12.470
In Eden, in Cumbria, just 25.5
people live on each square kilometre.

3
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:17.210
In London, it's 5,597.6.

4
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:23.030
In Tower Hamlets, the
densest district, 15,702.9.

5
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.490
So why is the UK's most crowded
corner classed as water-stressed?

6
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.510
Does it never rain there?

7
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.070
Does the rain all run into the sea?

8
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.870
In this mission, you'll map
where the UK's people live,

9
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.290
and how its land is used.

10
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.790
Then you'll weigh two pressures
on the same crowded corner:

11
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.870
water, and homes.

12
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:47.490
Your mission: find out why the UK's most
crowded corner is classed as water-stressed.
